# Issue / PR branch workflow

When the user asks you to **implement, fix, or take care of** a GitHub issue or PR
(numbered issue, issue URL, or "fix #N"):

## Before editing any code

1. Run `git status -sb` and note the current branch.
2. **Ask the user** whether to create a new branch (use `AskQuestion` when available):

   - **Yes — create a branch** (recommended if on `main` or an unrelated branch)
   - **No — use current branch** (only if they are already on the right feature branch)
   - **I'll branch myself** — wait; do not edit until they confirm the branch name

3. Do **not** start file edits until they answer (unless they already said in the
   same message to create a branch or to use a named branch).

## If they want a new branch

1. `git fetch origin`
2. Base from `origin/main` unless they specify another base.
3. Branch name: `fix/<issue#>-<short-slug>` (e.g. `fix/19-account-settings-label-gap`).
4. Prefer linking on GitHub when an issue number is known:

   ```bash
   gh issue develop <N> -R TortoiseWolfe/RescueDogs --checkout --name fix/<N>-<short-slug>
   ```

   Fall back to `git checkout -b fix/<N>-<short-slug> origin/main` if `gh` fails.

5. Confirm the branch name in chat before implementing.

## Guardrails

- Never commit directly to `main`.
- One issue per branch when possible; do not mix unrelated work.
- Commits and pushes only when the user asks (per user rules).
